WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.105
The federal requirement, from NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three,

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.475
revision five, as the guide's
requirements table maps it.

3
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:14.333
Step 1 supports C M two, baseline
configuration, C M six, configuration settings,

4
00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:17.037
and C A seven, continuous monitoring,

5
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:22.625
aligned with the fed-ramp twenty X key
security indicators the guide names.

6
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:26.850
The evidence is the initiative
assignments and the compliance export.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:32.440
Step 2 supports C M eight, system component
inventory, and S C seven, boundary

8
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:38.662
protection; its evidence is the dated
register, reconciled with Defender for Cloud.

9
00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:40.738
The steps support these controls.

10
00:00:40.738 --> 00:00:43.561
The organization still
sets their parameters,

11
00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:46.675
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

12
00:00:46.675 --> 00:00:50.829
The key security indicators are
written for cloud service providers;

13
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:53.620
the agency lines its own
evidence up with them.
